# E §11 (tally 2.1.3, issue #58): "`REQ-ASK` | the request names an ask that doesn't exist | the request is refused,
# after load (a load refusal outranks it), in every shape of reality ...: `no ask <q>`". The reality loads; the request
# names zz, which no file declares, so the run prints the one refusal. Was `refused: LOAD-NAME no ask zz` (refcore's
# own code; T's SR-1).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input y: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  y = 1

ask q: y
=== expect zz
refused: REQ-ASK no ask zz
